+**State/locking design:** the persisted judged-run manifest is authoritative for the single immutable attempt (`attempt: 1`); the valid audit chain must contain exactly one terminal event for that run/attempt, and it must be a completion matching the manifest and output evidence for the run to be accepted. Legal progression is `pending_approval` → `finalizing` → `completed`, `pending_approval` → `rejected`, or any nonterminal attempt → `failed`; terminal attempts do not transition to another terminal state. A same-run failed attempt is not retried in place. Recovery may reconcile `finalizing` to `completed` only when persisted approval, sources, artifact, audit export and audit evidence all verify and no terminal history exists; otherwise it fails closed. A lock conflict returns busy/in-progress without changing the manifest.
+
+`withJudgedRunLock` serializes API preparation, approval decision plus finalization, resume/recovery, and CLI/dashboard T-07 execution. Its per-run lock is an atomic same-directory hard-link on the canonical real project root, shared across local processes; T-07 also takes a shared-output lock. Acquisition/reclamation failure never falls through to unlocked mutation. Recovery only reclaims a same-host lock when its PID is demonstrably gone; live, foreign-host, malformed or otherwise uncertain locks remain busy/unavailable. There is no age-only lease stealing. This supports local single-host filesystems that provide same-directory hard links, not multi-host/network coordination. PID reuse or a process crash while holding the reclaim marker can cause a conservative manual-inspection/busy condition.
